        {
          "type": "grid",
          "cards": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "Charge control",
              "icon": "mdi:tune-variant",
              "heading_style": "title"
            },
            {
              "type": "entities",
              "entities": [
                {
                  "entity": "number.living_room_sh_453ab4_maximum_charge",
                  "name": "Maximum charge"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "number.living_room_sh_453ab4_minimum_charge",
                  "name": "Minimum charge"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "number.living_room_sh_453ab4_additional_charge",
                  "name": "Additional charge (hours)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "divider"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "switch.living_room_sh_453ab4_smart_charging",
                  "name": "Rointe's smart charging"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "switch.living_room_sh_453ab4_boost",
                  "name": "Boost"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "**Smart charging on** — the heater decides how much it needs within the\nhours you allow. Right for Economy 7, where the cheap window never moves.\n\n**Smart charging off** — the schedule you write is authoritative. Right for a\nhalf-hourly tariff, where Home Assistant picks the hours. Set *additional\ncharge* to 0 at the same time, or it may take up to that many hours at\nwhatever the price happens to be."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "Economy 7 window",
              "heading_style": "subtitle"
            },
            {
              "type": "entities",
              "entities": [
                {
                  "entity": "input_datetime.economy7_start",
                  "name": "Cheap rate starts"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "input_datetime.economy7_end",
                  "name": "Cheap rate ends"
                },
                {
                  "entity": "binary_sensor.economy_7_window",
                  "name": "Cheap rate now"
                }
              ],
              "footer": {
                "type": "graph",
                "entity": "sensor.living_room_sh_453ab4_charge",
                "hours_to_show": 24
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "Set these to the times your meter actually switches — everything else on this dashboard keys off them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "grid",
          "cards": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "heading": "Diagnostics",
              "icon": "mdi:stethoscope",
              "heading_style": "title"
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "binary_sensor.living_room_sh_453ab4_online",
              "name": "Cloud connection"
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "binary_sensor.living_room_sh_453ab4_open_window_detected",
              "name": "Open window detected"
            },
            {
              "type": "tile",
              "entity": "sensor.living_room_heater_charge_energy",
              "name": "Energy since setup (est.)"
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "### Writing a charge window\n\n```yaml\naction: rointe_nexa.set_charge_hours\ntarget:\n  entity_id: climate.living_room_sh_453ab4\ndata:\n  hours: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]   # each hour it MAY charge\n  days: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]       # Mon-Fri, omit for every day\n```\n\nHour numbers are the hour that *starts* then, so `[2]` means 02:00–03:00.\nCommands are zone-scoped: two heaters in one Nexa zone share settings, so\ngive each its own zone in the app."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
